PS5 HDMI: 4K120 over HDMI 2.1 FRL on FLAVA3 (Lawson), hdmi.frl_4k120

Ported from Lawson's PS5 kernel (vrr13), which follows how Sony's 13.60 kernel programs
the FLAVA3 chip for its 4K120 mode (mode id 211; 4K100, 210, isn't offered):
 - VIC 118 gets Sony's 4K120 mode index (0x7227/0x7070 = 0x0b) and its own
   basic-config tail (0x7070 = VIC VIC 00, 0x7074 = 00, 0x7203 = 60, 0x7011 = d5)
 - after the PHY setup: the "SCEI"/"PS5" SPD, and event sequence 0x30 (registered with
   4/16), which the chip runs when the FRL link is up: AVI with the VIC, IT content, game
 - the additional config in its FRL variant: no TMDS scrambling/SCDC, output started
   with 5/3 02, after which the chip trains the FRL link itself
 - the GPU-to-chip DP link (HBR3 x4) carries 4K120 as YCbCr 4:2:2, amdgpu's own encoding
   fallback when RGB doesn't fit
In FRL modes the setup skips the stock PHY tail and VSync block that VRR needs on TMDS
(v1.7.1): Lawson's 4K120 VRR ran on Sony's FRL setup without them.
Offered on FLAVA3 when the TV lists 4K120 itself; hdmi.frl_4k120=0 never offers it.
